<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's AFMC buys 20,000T of U.S. No.1 soybean.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's AFMC buys 20,000T of U.S. No.1 soybean.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's state-run Agricultural &amp; Fishery Marketing Corporation (AFMC) said on Friday it bought 20,000 tonnes of U.S. No 1 soybean at $338.27 per tonne, C&amp;F.  </p>
<p>A senior official at the AFMC said Daewoo International (America) Corp won the contract with shipment for September 26-October 15 if from the U.S. Gulf or for October 11-30 if from the Pacific Northwest.</p>
<p>Arrival was set for the western port city of Inchon by November 20.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
